"fetchedAt":"2026-09-17T15:38:32+00:00","id":"sjres45-119","introducedDate":"2025-04-04","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-04-04","text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Environment and Public Works."},"laws":[],"number":"45","originChamber":"Senate","policyArea":"Environmental Protection","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"C001047","district":null,"fullName":"Sen. Capito, Shelley Moore [R-WV]","party":"R","state":"WV"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-04-04","actionDesc":"Introduced in Senate","text":"<p>This joint resolution nullifies the Environmental Protection Agency notice titled <em>California State Motor Vehicle and Engine Pollution Control Standards; Advanced Clean Cars II; Waiver of Preemption; Notice of Decision</em> (90 Fed. Reg. 642) and published on January 6, 2025. Among other elements, the notice grants the California Air Resources Board request for a waiver for its Advanced Clean Cars II (ACC II) regulations. (Under the Clean Air Act, California may seek waivers of the preemption prohibiting states from enacting certain emission standards.)&nbsp;</p>","updateDate":"2025-06-11T14:35:45Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"A joint resolution providing for congressional disapproval under chapter 8 of title 5, United States Code, of the rule submitted by the Environmental Protection Agency relating to \"California State Motor Vehicle and Engine Pollution Control Standards; Advanced Clean Cars II; Waiver of Preemption; Notice of Decision\".","type":"sjres","updateDate":"2026-09-08T18:12:22Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-08T18:12:22Z"}
